body:
It seems this isn't a problem with the health check implementation, but rather a problem with the pool injection.

Consider this:

```java
	@Inject
	private io.vertx.mutiny.pgclient.PgPool mutinyPool;
	@Inject
	private io.vertx.pgclient.PgPool pool;

	@PostConstruct
	protected void init() {
		System.out.println("pool = " + pool);
		System.out.println("mutinyPool.getDelegate() = " + mutinyPool.getDelegate());
	}
```

The output will be something like:

```
pool = io.vertx.pgclient.impl.PgPoolImpl@6a6aea13
mutinyPool.getDelegate() = io.vertx.pgclient.impl.PgPoolImpl@37d7bd79
```

But it should be:

```
pool = io.vertx.pgclient.impl.PgPoolImpl@6a6aea13
mutinyPool.getDelegate() = io.vertx.pgclient.impl.PgPoolImpl@6a6aea13
```

In other words, Quarkus creates two different pools if both the Mutiny and Vert.x variants are injected.

@geoand I'm not sure, but I suspect this might be related to https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/commit/dc78468f027944b66396fd5b89abd111e219e54a

Would you mind taking a look?

Can you please try this:

1. create a new project with https://code.quarkus.io/?j=21&e=reactive-pg-client&extension-search=origin:platform%20postgres
2. add the class below to the project
3.  run

```java
import io.quarkus.runtime.Startup;
import jakarta.annotation.PostConstruct;
import jakarta.inject.Inject;
import jakarta.inject.Singleton;

@Singleton
@Startup
public class Test {

    @Inject
    io.vertx.mutiny.pgclient.PgPool mutinyPool;
    @Inject
    io.vertx.pgclient.PgPool pool;

    @PostConstruct
    protected void init() {
        System.out.println("pool = " + pool);
        System.out.println("mutinyPool.getDelegate() = " + mutinyPool.getDelegate());
    }

}
```

I get this on the console:

```
pool = io.vertx.pgclient.impl.PgPoolImpl@795fb3c5
mutinyPool.getDelegate() = io.vertx.pgclient.impl.PgPoolImpl@41c8893a
```
